Sales
  Data Science: Optimizing Sales
    Visit Webiste -> Product Page -> Shopping cart -> Checkout
  Machine Learning: 
    Prioritize sales contacts that have the power and money to buy products from your           company: 
        Name    Title    Company Size    Email          Priority
        Taylor   CEO        3050         tay@gmail.com    High
        Janet    Manager    230          jan@yahoo.com    Medium
        David    Intern     30           dave@aol.com     LOW

        ML can analyze this data and find that David would not be a good person to                contact about selling large amounts of products as he is an intern and is in a            smaller company. 
        Taylor, however, should be contacted as they are a CEO and part of a big company. 
      This is called Automated Lead Sorting that makes the sales force more effcient. 

Manufacturing Line Manager
  Data Science: Optimize Manufacturing
    Mix Clay -> Shape Mug -> Add Glaze -> Fire Kiln -> Final Inspection
  Machine Learning: 
    Take a data set of Input A: Pictures of mug and find Input B: whether they are ok to       sell or have defects and need to be scrapped. 
    This called automated visual inspection. 
        Can decrease labor costs and improve factory quality. 

Recruiting
  Data Science: Optimizing Recruiting Funnel
    Email Outreach -> Phone Screen -> Onsite Interview -> Offer
  Machine Learning: 
    Screen resumes: Input A Resume and Pick the candidates who have a Bachelors degree or       higher in a specific field. 
    This is called Automated Resume Screening.

Marketing
Data Science: A/B Testing
  Testing two websites, ads, promotions, etc and seeing which is utilized more.
Machine Learning: 
  A model would analyze a user's shopping patterns or interest (how often user views or       buys product) and eventualy would start showing user adds for that specific product        they were thinking of purchasing. 
  This is called customized product reccommendations
      It drives a lot sales for large online e-commerce websites

Agriculture
Data Science: Crop Analytics
  Take data from soil and weeather conditions, presence of different crops in the market     and make decisions for what and when to plant crops and how to improve crops' quality. 
Machine Learning: 
  Input A: Picture of soil
  Input B: AI selecting which plant in the picture is a weed. 
  This is also used on plants so the plant-owners can take pictures of their plants and       understand if the plant hase too much sunlight, not enough water, etc. based on the        condition of the plant in the picture. 
  This is called Precision Weed Killing   
